# project-memory/

Durable engineering memory — the *why* the dashboard would lose if rewritten.

| File | Admit only if… |
|---|---|
| `architecture.md` | forgetting it would cause a wrong code change |
| `decisions.md` | likely to be re-argued, with the rejection's measurement or incident |
| `experiments.md` | the number affects a threshold / baseline / closure |

5–10 lines per entry; rule first, then `Why:` and `How to apply:`; link docs instead of
compressing them; supersede, don't delete. Full rules: the `file-based-memory` skill's
`references/memory-model.md`. Checkpoint with `/file-based-memory:save-status`.
